{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"515","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Drazil and Tiles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Drazil created a following problem about putting "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 × 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" tiles into an "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" grid:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"There is a grid with some cells that are empty and some cells that are occupied. You should use "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 × 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" tiles to cover all empty cells and no two tiles should cover each other. And you should print a solution about how to do it.\""}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"But Drazil doesn't like to write special checking program for this task. His friend, Varda advised him: \"how about asking contestant only to print the solution "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"when it exists and it is unique"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"? Otherwise contestant may print '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Not unique"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' \"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Drazil found that the constraints for this task may be much larger than for the original task!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you solve this new problem?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that you should print '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Not unique"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' either when there exists no solution or when there exists several different solutions for the original task."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 2000"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the grid rows. Character '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' denotes an empty cell, and the character '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"*"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' denotes a cell that is occupied."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there is no solution or the solution is not unique, you should print the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Not unique"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise you should print how to cover all empty cells with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 × 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" tiles. Use characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"<>"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" to denote horizontal tiles and characters \"^v\" to denote vertical tiles. Refer to the sample test for the output format example."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3\n...\n.*.\n...\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"Not unique\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 4\n..**\n*...\n*.**\n....\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"<>**\n*^<>\n*v**\n<><>\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 4\n*..*\n....\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"*<>*\n<><>\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n.\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"Not unique\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n*\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"*\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first case, there are indeed two solutions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n<>^\n^*v\nv<>\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n^<>\nv*^\n<>v\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"so the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Not unique"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"515D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/515/problem/D"}